        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="NestedObject">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Nesting is used to fully describe the single instance of the secondary entity which is referenced by the primary entity</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="DescriptiveReference">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Nesting is used to partially describe the single instance of the secondary entity which is referenced by the primary entity.  The nested item is a &quot;reference&quot; which holds more than just an identifier - it also contains some additional information about the referenced object, with the aim of reducing the need for the secondary entity to be fetched separately.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="Subtype">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>The secondary entity extends the primary entity, providing additional information that is relevant to a particular of that entity.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="UniqueChild">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>A single instance of the secondary entity is nested within the primary entity</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="PassThrough">
        <xs:annotation>
